---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import InstallTabs from '../components/InstallTabs.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Install" active="install" description="Install all three CLIs in under two minutes — pipx for nda-review-cli, npm for sign-cli and docx2pdf-cli." toc>
  <p class="eyebrow">Install</p>
  <h1>Three installs, one workflow.</h1>

  <p class="text-lg text-ink-700 dark:text-night-100">
    Each CLI is a standalone package on its native registry. Install whichever ones you need;
    they don't depend on each other and there's no shared runtime to set up.
  </p>

  <Callout label="TL;DR">
    <code class="chip">pipx install nda-review-cli</code> · <code class="chip">npm i -g docx2pdf-cli</code> · <code class="chip">npm i -g sign-cli</code>.
    Verify with <code class="chip">--version</code> on each.
  </Callout>

  <h2>Prerequisites</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Python 3.9+</strong> with <code class="chip">pipx</code> for nda-review-cli. Install pipx via <code class="chip">brew install pipx</code> or your distro package manager, then <code class="chip">pipx ensurepath</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Node.js 18+</strong> for sign-cli and docx2pdf-cli. Install via <code class="chip">brew install node</code>, <code class="chip">nvm</code>, or your platform's installer.</li>
    <li><strong>A PDF backend</strong> (only for docx2pdf-cli) — LibreOffice, Microsoft Word, Pandoc, or a Gotenberg server. The tool auto-detects what's installed.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>nda-review-cli</h2>
  <p>The Python CLI for drafting, reviewing, and negotiating NDAs. Stdlib-only at runtime — pipx installs it cleanly into its own environment.</p>

  <InstallTabs
    id="nda-tabs"
    tabs={[
      { id: 'pipx', label: 'pipx', command: 'pipx install nda-review-cli\nnda-review-cli --version', note: 'Recommended — isolates dependencies and adds the CLI to your $PATH.' },
      { id: 'pip',  label: 'pip',  command: 'pip install --user nda-review-cli', note: 'Use if you don\'t have pipx. Make sure ~/.local/bin is on your $PATH.' },
      { id: 'src',  label: 'from source', command: 'git clone https://github.com/DrBaher/nda-review-cli.git\ncd nda-review-cli && ./nda_review_cli.py --help', note: 'Single-file stdlib-only Python — runs straight from a clone.' },
    ]}
  />

  <CodeBlock label="first-run setup">{`# 16 quick questions write your house policy
nda-review-cli quickstart`}</CodeBlock>

  <h2>docx2pdf-cli</h2>
  <p>The Node.js CLI for DOCX → PDF conversion with hybrid backends.</p>

  <InstallTabs
    id="d2p-tabs"
    tabs={[
      { id: 'npm',  label: 'npm',  command: 'npm i -g docx2pdf-cli\ndocx2pdf --version' },
      { id: 'pnpm', label: 'pnpm', command: 'pnpm add -g docx2pdf-cli' },
      { id: 'yarn', label: 'yarn', command: 'yarn global add docx2pdf-cli' },
      { id: 'npx',  label: 'npx',  command: 'npx docx2pdf-cli@latest --doctor', note: 'No install — runs the latest version once.' },
    ]}
  />

  <CodeBlock label="sanity check">{`# Probe what backends are detected on this machine
docx2pdf --doctor
docx2pdf --list-backends`}</CodeBlock>

  <p>
    The <code class="chip">--doctor</code> probe walks every backend candidate (LibreOffice, Word,
    Pandoc, Gotenberg) and reports which ones are usable. Pick one with <code class="chip">--backend</code>
    or let the tool auto-select.
  </p>

  <h2>sign-cli</h2>
  <p>The TypeScript CLI for multi-provider e-signature with audit trails.</p>

  <InstallTabs
    id="sign-tabs"
    tabs={[
      { id: 'npm',  label: 'npm',  command: 'npm i -g sign-cli\nsign-cli --version' },
      { id: 'pnpm', label: 'pnpm', command: 'pnpm add -g sign-cli' },
      { id: 'yarn', label: 'yarn', command: 'yarn global add sign-cli' },
      { id: 'npx',  label: 'npx',  command: 'npx sign-cli@latest demo', note: 'One-shot offline demo — no install required.' },
    ]}
  />

  <p>
    The offline demo walks the full flow (send → token → sign → verify → receipt) using a built-in
    local provider — no signup, no third-party calls, ~5 seconds end to end.
  </p>

  <h2>Configuration locations</h2>
  <p>Each tool keeps its config in standard places. Nothing is shared across tools.</p>
  <table class="not-prose mt-4 w-full border-collapse text-[14px]">
    <thead>
      <tr class="border-b border-ink-700/15 text-left dark:border-night-300/20">
        <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-night-50">Tool</th>
        <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-night-50">Config</th>
        <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-night-50">Sensitive bits</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="text-ink-700 dark:text-night-100">
      <tr class="border-b border-ink-700/10 dark:border-night-300/15">
        <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono">nda-review-cli</td>
        <td class="py-2 pr-4"><code class="chip">config/org-policy.json</code>, <code class="chip">profiles/</code>, optional <code class="chip">config/llm.json</code></td>
        <td class="py-2 pr-4">LLM provider keys (gitignored)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr class="border-b border-ink-700/10 dark:border-night-300/15">
        <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono">docx2pdf-cli</td>
        <td class="py-2 pr-4">Optional <code class="chip">.docx2pdfrc</code></td>
        <td class="py-2 pr-4">Gotenberg URL if remote backend in use</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono">sign-cli</td>
        <td class="py-2 pr-4"><code class="chip">~/.config/sign-cli/</code> or env vars</td>
        <td class="py-2 pr-4">Provider API keys (Dropbox Sign, DocuSign, SignWell)</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Updating</h2>
  <CodeBlock>{`pipx upgrade nda-review-cli
npm update -g docx2pdf-cli sign-cli`}</CodeBlock>

  <h2>Uninstalling</h2>
  <p>
    Each tool comes off cleanly. There are no daemons, services, or system-wide modifications to
    clean up afterwards.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock>{`pipx uninstall nda-review-cli
npm rm -g docx2pdf-cli sign-cli`}</CodeBlock>
</BaseLayout>
